# Schemas
# Pydantic models that define the shape of data crossing the API boundary.
# They are the contract between the frontend and backend — what the request body
# must look like, and what the response will always look like.
# Keeping these separate from models/ means you can change your DB internals
# without breaking the API contract (and vice versa).
# Example: schemas/document.py will define DocumentCreateRequest and DocumentResponse.
